<title>MEXICO: Mexico stocks break 4,000-point barrier.</title>
<headline>Mexico stocks break 4,000-point barrier.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican stocks on Thursday afternoon broke the 4,000-point barrier for the first time, as gains by media heavyweight Grupo Televisa SA and slow, steady improvement in the economic picture helped lift the market, dealers said.</p>
<p>The IPC index was at 4,000.85 points, up 26.43 points, or 0.67 percent, in late trade, though volume was weaker than usual at 65.35 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Finally, we reach 4,000 points. We were close, so some people bought blue chips to push it over,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
</text>
